WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:02.009
SPEAKER: Hello, and
welcome to Cloud Minute.

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:05.010
Today I'm going to talk about
managing SSH keys on Google

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:06.930
Compute Engine instances.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.670
One of the challenges
many teams face

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.580
is controlling who has SSH
access to their Compute Engine

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.679
resources.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.970
There are a lot of ways to
do this with code, including

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.064
various groups and tools.

00:00:16.064 --> 00:00:18.480
But Compute Engine provides a
way to do it from the web UI

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.470
as well.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:27.250
From Google Cloud Console,
click Compute Engine, Metadata.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.180
And then click SSH Keys.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:32.310
Now, to add an SSH
key, I click here.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.700
You paste the whole key
in, and you click Save.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.360
And the SSH keys
are propagated out

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.410
to all the Compute Engine
resources in your project.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:41.480
Let's test it out.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.190
And you can see I have SSH
access to that Compute Engine

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.140
resource.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.070
When it comes time to revoke the
key, click Edit, click the X,

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.510
and then click Save.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.110
And now you see I get a
Permission Denied error.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:58.870
So if you've been struggling to
control or audit the SSH access

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.560
to your project, try this out.

